WEBVTT

00:00:12.970 --> 00:00:14.300
Did it run aground there?

00:00:14.380 --> 00:00:17.050
It doesn't look like
an abandoned ship from the old world.

00:00:17.140 --> 00:00:18.470
Want to take a closer look?

00:00:18.930 --> 00:00:20.970
No, it might be a trap.

00:00:21.350 --> 00:00:23.060
What? Whose trap?

00:00:23.310 --> 00:00:25.310
I'm willing to bet you never saw it,

00:00:25.940 --> 00:00:31.440
but during our test, I had to deal
with some trouble on a ship like that.

00:00:32.030 --> 00:00:33.030
Let's just wait and see.

00:02:07.830 --> 00:02:09.460
SUMMER BEGINS

00:02:14.130 --> 00:02:15.300
Hey, Natsu!

00:02:15.380 --> 00:02:16.550
You've got to sing too!

00:02:16.630 --> 00:02:18.130
And do the dance!

00:02:18.220 --> 00:02:20.760
Move those hips more. Like this.

00:02:22.010 --> 00:02:23.850
I can't dance like this.

00:02:23.930 --> 00:02:25.060
You dummy!

00:02:25.180 --> 00:02:30.190
We have to master this comedy routine
to win the talent show on Sunday.

00:02:30.270 --> 00:02:31.900
Okay, let's start over.

00:02:33.480 --> 00:02:37.150
Howdy!
Welcome to the Semimaru and Natsu show!

00:02:37.360 --> 00:02:38.530
Hey, Natsu.

00:02:38.610 --> 00:02:41.820
"Aloha" is what they say
to greet people in Hawaii, right?

00:02:42.070 --> 00:02:44.330
But then, what does "oe" mean?

00:02:45.870 --> 00:02:47.370
I said, what does "oe" mean?

00:02:50.290 --> 00:02:51.580
It doesn't mean to puke!

00:02:51.670 --> 00:02:53.960
Quit it! That's rude to Hawaiians!

00:02:55.300 --> 00:02:56.550
It's not a dolphin either!

00:02:56.630 --> 00:02:59.260
Oh, that might work.

00:03:01.220 --> 00:03:03.890
Okay, let's work on even more gags!

00:03:03.970 --> 00:03:05.720
You come up with some ideas too.

00:03:05.810 --> 00:03:08.100
-I've made up our entire routine!
-This is obviously a trap.

00:03:08.180 --> 00:03:09.310
-Right.
-I'm sorry.

00:03:11.310 --> 00:03:13.810
It looks like he's grinding something up.

00:03:21.650 --> 00:03:23.660
Look. There's more of them in the water.

00:03:25.280 --> 00:03:28.040
Ms. Botan,
do you think this might be edible?

00:03:28.120 --> 00:03:31.540
I'm ready to try anything.
I'll go ahead and taste it.

00:03:31.620 --> 00:03:33.750
If it turns out to be poisonous,
then I'm just unlucky.

00:03:33.830 --> 00:03:37.090
You don't have to worry.
I get the feeling we're lucky.

00:03:37.670 --> 00:03:40.220
Look, they laid a trap just for you.

00:03:40.630 --> 00:03:44.050
Ryo, I keep telling you,
I don't actually want to assault women.

00:03:44.260 --> 00:03:47.220
Obviously, because only idiots do that.

00:03:48.220 --> 00:03:49.600
I get it already.

00:03:50.180 --> 00:03:52.690
Ms. Botan,
please put a top on or something.

00:03:52.770 --> 00:03:55.020
Why don't you just get used to it?

00:03:55.100 --> 00:03:56.190
No way!

00:03:57.400 --> 00:04:00.490
-What's that?
-Is it a kitchen sink?

00:04:01.070 --> 00:04:03.610
The ocean around here is
filled with treasure.

00:04:04.320 --> 00:04:06.450
Maybe it's not a good idea
to rely on antiques, but...

00:04:06.530 --> 00:04:08.240
We should make use of whatever we can.

00:04:09.240 --> 00:04:11.120
I have no idea what they're talking about.

00:04:11.540 --> 00:04:14.120
Daily quotas and crisis management,
probably.

00:04:15.710 --> 00:04:17.130
There are seven of them.

00:04:17.340 --> 00:04:20.880
I guess this must be
the other Team Summer.

00:04:21.210 --> 00:04:22.260
What do we do?

00:04:22.340 --> 00:04:25.130
I doubt that ship will sail,
so there's no point in stealing it.

00:04:25.550 --> 00:04:27.470
Plus, it's possible
they've got guns like us.

00:04:28.350 --> 00:04:32.140
If this team was made to counter ours,
then they should be very skilled.

00:04:32.890 --> 00:04:34.690
For now, we watch from a distance.

00:04:37.020 --> 00:04:38.560
I'm going to crash!

00:04:48.700 --> 00:04:50.290
Thanks.

00:04:51.490 --> 00:04:52.870
No way!

00:04:52.950 --> 00:04:54.910
Oh, my god! Two total hunks!

00:04:55.210 --> 00:04:58.040
My dreams are coming true! Awesome!

00:04:58.130 --> 00:05:00.750
Two princes came just to rescue me.

00:05:02.460 --> 00:05:04.130
Chimackie!

00:05:04.630 --> 00:05:05.680
Look.

00:05:05.760 --> 00:05:07.430
I found two hunks!

00:05:07.890 --> 00:05:09.930
Oh, wow. Hello there.

00:05:10.010 --> 00:05:13.430
Hey. I thought your plan was
to keep our distance.

00:05:13.520 --> 00:05:14.430
Too late for that now.

00:05:14.520 --> 00:05:16.730
I just know this must be fate!

00:05:17.850 --> 00:05:19.770
Good for you, Matsuri.

00:05:19.860 --> 00:05:23.190
Don't go blabbing all about
our past this time, okay?

00:05:23.610 --> 00:05:25.400
-It puts us at a disadvantage.
-Right.

00:05:25.490 --> 00:05:26.820
I won't screw up again.

00:05:33.200 --> 00:05:37.170
Check it out, Nat!
We finally found some real hunks!

00:05:37.250 --> 00:05:40.340
What do you mean, Matsuri?
Arashi and I have always been here!

00:05:40.960 --> 00:05:42.130
What is this "hunk" thing?

00:05:42.210 --> 00:05:43.340
No clue.

00:05:43.420 --> 00:05:46.130
This is a surprise. Who are you, boys?

00:05:46.670 --> 00:05:48.550
We're all from Team Summer B.

00:05:49.550 --> 00:05:50.550
We're Summer.

00:05:51.800 --> 00:05:54.270
You mean Summer A? Really?

00:05:54.350 --> 00:05:55.310
Seriously?

00:05:55.390 --> 00:05:57.230
It's about time we met our buddies.

00:05:57.810 --> 00:06:00.560
I've heard yours was
the first team they ever put together.

00:06:00.860 --> 00:06:02.190
It's so great to meet you.

00:06:02.820 --> 00:06:03.820
Are you two alone?

00:06:04.150 --> 00:06:05.440
What about your other members?

00:06:06.490 --> 00:06:07.320
We got separated.

00:06:07.400 --> 00:06:08.860
That's not good.

00:06:09.030 --> 00:06:10.320
We'll help you find them.

00:06:10.870 --> 00:06:13.030
It's fine. They're not nearby.

00:06:14.410 --> 00:06:15.450
Excuse me.

00:06:15.540 --> 00:06:18.290
It's almost time for the usual, everyone.

00:06:18.370 --> 00:06:20.290
Oh, it's already that late?

00:06:20.370 --> 00:06:21.580
Soap! Got to get soap!

00:06:21.670 --> 00:06:24.170
-Grab the pots and kettles!
-Get ready!

00:06:24.750 --> 00:06:25.670
Here it comes.

00:06:25.760 --> 00:06:28.300
Three, two, one!

00:06:33.430 --> 00:06:34.510
A geyser.

00:06:34.600 --> 00:06:36.060
And it's a cold one.

00:06:36.220 --> 00:06:37.310
That's rare.

00:06:37.390 --> 00:06:39.270
It erupts five times a day.

00:06:39.350 --> 00:06:42.190
We tried to bring the ship close
after we saw it,

00:06:42.270 --> 00:06:44.480
but it got stuck on the rocks.

00:06:45.690 --> 00:06:48.360
This group is completely vulnerable.

00:06:48.740 --> 00:06:49.860
It certainly seems that way.

00:06:49.950 --> 00:06:52.740
The only one with any training
is the guide, Botan.

00:06:52.820 --> 00:06:54.160
Her muscles are well toned.

00:06:54.450 --> 00:06:56.080
She's attentive and guarded.

00:06:56.160 --> 00:06:57.410
Arashi too.

00:06:57.660 --> 00:06:59.330
He looks highly athletic.

00:06:59.870 --> 00:07:01.670
The rest of them are pathetic.

00:07:01.750 --> 00:07:02.750
Particularly Natsu.

00:07:02.830 --> 00:07:03.960
Is this intentional?

00:07:04.460 --> 00:07:05.920
Are they just testing us?

00:07:12.550 --> 00:07:14.800
You're the guide of this group, right?

00:07:15.430 --> 00:07:17.140
Are you allied with the professors?

00:07:18.060 --> 00:07:22.270
I used to be a police officer before.
Is your guide a professor?

00:07:24.230 --> 00:07:26.980
I heard the guides were civil servants,

00:07:27.070 --> 00:07:28.780
so it makes sense
that there is a professor.

00:07:29.240 --> 00:07:31.820
I would really love to meet them
at some point.

00:07:33.240 --> 00:07:34.910
All right, the tide's gone out!

00:07:34.990 --> 00:07:36.620
Let's go and grab our dinner!

00:07:37.490 --> 00:07:38.620
Do you guys want to join us?

00:07:39.000 --> 00:07:40.750
We'll show you around the ship.

00:07:43.880 --> 00:07:47.210
They both seem like really calm
and level-headed people to me.

00:07:48.550 --> 00:07:50.300
They're leaving a lot of room.

00:07:50.550 --> 00:07:51.380
"Room"?

00:07:51.470 --> 00:07:54.090
They're intentionally keeping
their distance from us,

00:07:54.180 --> 00:07:56.260
to make sure they can respond
in case we do anything.

00:07:57.050 --> 00:07:59.140
They might be trained in martial arts.

00:07:59.720 --> 00:08:02.850
Seeing them all rigid and nervous
like that, it's honestly adorable.

00:08:02.940 --> 00:08:05.350
Ms. Botan, are you a man-eater?

00:08:05.940 --> 00:08:06.980
"Man-eater"?

00:08:08.150 --> 00:08:09.940
We've got another rival.

00:08:10.780 --> 00:08:11.740
Listen, Nat.

00:08:11.820 --> 00:08:14.990
No matter who ends up with who,
we're still friends, okay?

00:08:15.070 --> 00:08:16.030
What?

00:08:16.120 --> 00:08:18.240
I'm not into...

00:08:18.330 --> 00:08:21.950
Arashi already has a girlfriend,
so you have to find somebody else.

00:08:22.910 --> 00:08:24.290
But I'm not...

00:08:24.620 --> 00:08:25.920
I mean, I don't...

00:08:26.000 --> 00:08:28.340
It's obvious to see how you feel, Nat.

00:08:28.420 --> 00:08:29.840
I do not.

00:08:30.460 --> 00:08:32.220
<i>I can't even imagine it.</i>

00:08:32.880 --> 00:08:37.850
<i>There's no way anybody could fall in love
with someone like me.</i>

00:08:43.020 --> 00:08:44.810
Get them! Grab every last crab!

00:08:46.730 --> 00:08:48.440
It's an all-you-can-eat buffet!

00:08:48.730 --> 00:08:50.150
Semimaru, look behind you.

00:08:50.230 --> 00:08:51.190
What?

00:08:52.570 --> 00:08:54.860
Stay away! Don't get any closer!

00:08:58.490 --> 00:09:00.200
So you don't eat those kinds?

00:09:00.280 --> 00:09:02.250
Who eats weird shit like that?

00:09:04.830 --> 00:09:06.080
Hey, Arashi.

00:09:06.830 --> 00:09:09.040
Those dudes whipped out those knives fast.

00:09:09.340 --> 00:09:10.840
Yes, that was impressive.

00:09:11.460 --> 00:09:12.590
They must be experienced.

00:09:12.670 --> 00:09:13.800
Dumbass!

00:09:13.880 --> 00:09:15.550
We have to keep our eyes on them.

00:09:16.130 --> 00:09:18.720
When you've been around the block
as much as I have...

00:09:18.970 --> 00:09:21.560
I can tell that these guys aren't
really dangerous.

00:09:21.640 --> 00:09:25.140
Still, they might be here
to steal from us or something.

00:09:25.770 --> 00:09:27.900
Semimaru, have you forgotten?

00:09:28.810 --> 00:09:31.610
That's the same way
Team Autumn treated us when we met them.

00:09:32.360 --> 00:09:34.240
You thought that was unfair, didn't you?

00:09:34.900 --> 00:09:37.910
Look, all I'm saying is,
it's risky to trust them so easily.

00:09:38.200 --> 00:09:39.320
We need trust.

00:09:39.780 --> 00:09:41.280
What else is there in this world?

00:09:41.370 --> 00:09:43.450
Doesn't anyone clean or maintain this?

00:09:43.950 --> 00:09:45.160
It will get damaged quickly.

00:09:45.620 --> 00:09:49.380
If you leave the ship listing like this,
it will put undue pressure on the mast.

00:09:53.340 --> 00:09:55.300
Boy, I would love to tell my old self,

00:09:55.840 --> 00:09:58.220
"Guess what? You'll get sick of crabs!"

00:09:58.970 --> 00:10:00.890
Is that seasoning? Like sesame seeds?

00:10:00.970 --> 00:10:02.100
You've got some good stuff.

00:10:03.100 --> 00:10:04.100
It's a type of ant.

00:10:05.930 --> 00:10:07.600
Insects are the best source of protein.

00:10:08.350 --> 00:10:09.690
I've got sweet ones too.

00:10:12.900 --> 00:10:14.030
What do you think?

00:10:14.110 --> 00:10:16.030
Is this just a team of civilians,

00:10:16.490 --> 00:10:18.400
or were they specially chosen like us?

00:10:19.660 --> 00:10:22.990
They don't store any freshwater,
and they neglect their ship.

00:10:23.330 --> 00:10:25.910
They're afraid of bugs and animals
and can't deal with them.

00:10:27.080 --> 00:10:29.000
They're completely unprepared
if there's a crisis.

00:10:29.080 --> 00:10:31.040
Are they really another Team Summer?

00:10:31.130 --> 00:10:35.420
Remember what Ran said?
The reaper is likely part of Summer B.

00:10:36.050 --> 00:10:39.130
Is it Botan?
They called her a "man-eater" earlier.

00:10:40.300 --> 00:10:42.180
Should we do what Professor Takashi did?

00:10:42.720 --> 00:10:45.770
Get her in a chokehold and ask,
"How would you escape this?"

00:10:46.600 --> 00:10:49.310
Ryo. Don't say that name.

00:10:51.810 --> 00:10:52.810
Ever.

00:11:00.660 --> 00:11:02.370
<i>The waves are too noisy.</i>

00:11:02.870 --> 00:11:04.830
<i>It feels like something is
creeping up on me.</i>

00:11:06.240 --> 00:11:09.330
Well, it's about time for my shift.

00:11:13.080 --> 00:11:14.710
Where is Shigeru?

00:11:14.790 --> 00:11:15.710
Who?

00:11:15.800 --> 00:11:18.380
Where is Shigeru?

00:11:18.590 --> 00:11:19.800
I don't know.

00:11:23.760 --> 00:11:26.850
<i>Ango can't even hear the sound
of the waves crashing right now.</i>

00:11:27.600 --> 00:11:31.140
<i>Unlike Gengoro, he didn't do the deed
with his own two hands.</i>

00:11:31.520 --> 00:11:34.440
<i>And unlike Koruri, he never actually saw
the finality of death up close.</i>

00:11:35.400 --> 00:11:38.360
<i>To him,
the burden was just suddenly lifted.</i>

00:11:38.980 --> 00:11:40.190
<i>Gone without a trace.</i>

00:11:40.650 --> 00:11:41.610
<i>There was nothing more.</i>

00:11:41.700 --> 00:11:43.860
Hey, it's my turn.

00:11:44.820 --> 00:11:48.660
<i>His mind is still stuck in that damn test.</i>

00:11:48.740 --> 00:11:49.870
Go to bed.

00:11:53.960 --> 00:11:56.920
None of them are awake yet.
What the hell is going on?

00:11:57.340 --> 00:11:59.710
No, it looks like some are awake.

00:11:59.800 --> 00:12:03.300
Today is Saturday and tomorrow is Sunday!

00:12:03.380 --> 00:12:04.220
Saturday?

00:12:04.300 --> 00:12:08.890
Yes, that idiot Arashi decided we would be
better off with structure in our lives.

00:12:08.970 --> 00:12:12.640
We always do something special
on Sundays, so we're having a talent show.

00:12:13.020 --> 00:12:14.270
A talent show?

00:12:14.520 --> 00:12:16.860
I'm going to set up a stage
and decorate it a little.

00:12:16.940 --> 00:12:20.690
If you're free,
go pick up some sticks or whatever.

00:12:20.780 --> 00:12:21.650
"Whatever"?

00:12:21.740 --> 00:12:24.700
Yes, just some branches or grass,
whatever.

00:12:24.990 --> 00:12:26.240
What do you mean by "whatever"?

00:12:26.320 --> 00:12:27.200
What?

00:12:27.830 --> 00:12:29.490
Literally anything is fine, man.

00:12:29.580 --> 00:12:33.040
There are a lot of variables to consider,
like length and width.

00:12:33.210 --> 00:12:34.460
What do you mean by "whatever"?

00:12:34.540 --> 00:12:36.710
-Well, something suitable.
-"Suitable"?

00:12:37.380 --> 00:12:40.000
Look, just forget I asked.

00:12:40.590 --> 00:12:43.130
He must be the type
who takes everything seriously.

00:12:43.220 --> 00:12:44.130
Take this!

00:12:44.970 --> 00:12:46.050
That's cold!

00:12:46.180 --> 00:12:47.640
I'm not done yet!

00:12:47.720 --> 00:12:49.010
Take that!

00:12:49.100 --> 00:12:52.180
<i>None of them are assigned
a specific task for the day.</i>

00:12:53.640 --> 00:12:56.650
<i>They have a late breakfast
and dinner together.</i>

00:12:57.020 --> 00:12:59.190
<i>Aside from that,
each individual is free to eat whenever.</i>

00:12:59.270 --> 00:13:02.070
<i>And they prepare for
this "talent show" thing.</i>

00:13:02.150 --> 00:13:03.320
<i>What the hell is that?</i>

00:13:03.780 --> 00:13:05.990
<i>Don't they realize there are
more important things to do?</i>

00:13:06.320 --> 00:13:08.160
<i>There's a lot of work to be done.</i>

00:13:13.790 --> 00:13:15.160
The talent show...

00:13:15.750 --> 00:13:17.920
I really don't want to do it.

00:13:18.000 --> 00:13:18.960
So, is it just you?

00:13:19.460 --> 00:13:20.840
Are you the only one who works?

00:13:21.800 --> 00:13:23.460
I see you're not very good at it.

00:13:23.800 --> 00:13:25.170
You're really sloppy at it too.

00:13:26.180 --> 00:13:28.720
Well... I'm sorry.

00:13:29.760 --> 00:13:30.890
-Want some help?
-What?

00:13:30.970 --> 00:13:32.970
The sails need to be taken down
and mended.

00:13:33.470 --> 00:13:35.940
I can't do it with my injured hand,
so you do it.

00:13:36.390 --> 00:13:37.560
I'll do the cleaning instead.

00:13:37.980 --> 00:13:39.100
Give me that.

00:13:39.730 --> 00:13:40.730
Right.

00:13:42.150 --> 00:13:43.980
<i>He's really nice!</i>

00:13:46.990 --> 00:13:47.950
Ango?

00:13:51.330 --> 00:13:53.450
<i>Semimaru is making the best of things,
as usual.</i>

00:13:54.580 --> 00:13:56.790
<i>Ango has started to help Natsu out.</i>

00:13:57.080 --> 00:13:59.830
<i>I see his tendency
to look after others hasn't changed.</i>

00:14:00.920 --> 00:14:04.800
<i>What will Ryo and Ango think
after being exposed to Summer B?</i>

00:14:05.710 --> 00:14:07.220
<i>I expect they'll be surprised.</i>

00:14:09.430 --> 00:14:13.600
<i>But if they pose any threat,
then I'll know they're beyond saving.</i>

00:14:16.890 --> 00:14:18.600
<i>Ladies and men!</i>

00:14:18.690 --> 00:14:19.560
TALENT SHOW

00:14:19.650 --> 00:14:21.650
It's time for the weekly
Sunday night festivities!

00:14:21.730 --> 00:14:23.860
Tonight's entertainment is a talent show!

00:14:24.530 --> 00:14:27.190
Okay, the first to take the stage is
none other than us.

00:14:30.410 --> 00:14:32.700
Presenting Semimaru and Natsu.

00:14:35.700 --> 00:14:36.790
It doesn't mean "puke"!

00:14:36.870 --> 00:14:38.290
That's rude to Hawaiians!

00:14:40.040 --> 00:14:41.250
It's not a dolphin either!

00:14:41.330 --> 00:14:43.340
That's clearly a seal, not a dolphin!

00:14:43.420 --> 00:14:45.380
-You only got the letter "L" right.
-What?

00:14:46.760 --> 00:14:48.630
A seal and an elephant make
an elephant seal.

00:14:48.720 --> 00:14:50.970
A lion and a leopard make a leopon.

00:14:51.050 --> 00:14:51.970
What's the "pon"?

00:14:52.600 --> 00:14:53.430
A poncho!

00:14:55.850 --> 00:14:59.520
<i>What's going on?
He's staring at me so intently.</i>

00:15:00.190 --> 00:15:03.060
<i>Maybe he's really picky
about this type of comedy.</i>

00:15:03.150 --> 00:15:04.360
Stay focused!

00:15:04.440 --> 00:15:05.900
It's time for our big finish.

00:15:07.070 --> 00:15:09.280
I just noticed,
there's a big pile of seaweed right here!

00:15:09.360 --> 00:15:11.910
That's just my hair!

00:15:11.990 --> 00:15:14.160
-Thanks for watching!
-Thanks for watching!

00:15:15.580 --> 00:15:16.950
I don't get any of this.

00:15:17.040 --> 00:15:18.660
Don't think too hard about it.

00:15:23.750 --> 00:15:24.880
Looking cool, Big Sis!

00:15:24.960 --> 00:15:27.000
She might not make it with that chest.

00:15:27.590 --> 00:15:28.760
Flexibility training?

00:15:28.960 --> 00:15:30.510
I doubt it.

00:15:30.590 --> 00:15:32.340
I'll do a cheerleading routine

00:15:32.430 --> 00:15:35.720
while naming the 15 Tokugawa shoguns
in order!

00:15:37.810 --> 00:15:39.350
Ieyasu! Hidetada!

00:15:40.140 --> 00:15:42.650
Iemitsu! Yoshimune! Ietsugu! Ieharu!

00:15:42.730 --> 00:15:45.310
-She got the order wrong.
-Just leave it be.

00:15:45.400 --> 00:15:47.020
Oh, a magic trick?

00:15:47.650 --> 00:15:49.030
Ladder!

00:15:52.660 --> 00:15:53.820
Oh, jeez! Cat's cradle?

00:15:56.330 --> 00:15:59.910
Have any of you met
with the other teams yet?

00:16:00.000 --> 00:16:02.120
What's with the sudden questions?

00:16:02.460 --> 00:16:04.750
Semimaru, you guys met
some of the others, right?

00:16:05.210 --> 00:16:07.000
We sure did! We met Team Autumn.

00:16:07.380 --> 00:16:09.000
They're the absolute worst!

00:16:10.510 --> 00:16:12.050
They nearly killed us, right, Arashi?

00:16:12.130 --> 00:16:14.130
Because you tried to steal their food.

00:16:14.550 --> 00:16:17.510
Aside from them, we met
a cheeky little brat from Team Spring.

00:16:18.720 --> 00:16:20.810
And that dude with the pack of dogs.

00:16:21.480 --> 00:16:25.020
The survivor of Team Winter
who survived 15 years all by himself.

00:16:25.100 --> 00:16:27.360
He's pretty dangerous if you ask me.

00:16:27.440 --> 00:16:29.650
He looks harmless,
but appearances are deceiving.

00:16:31.320 --> 00:16:34.030
You're not wary of us?

00:16:34.660 --> 00:16:36.740
You don't seem like bad guys at all.

00:16:36.820 --> 00:16:39.030
You saved me from falling,
don't you remember?

00:16:39.120 --> 00:16:41.370
I know that boys your age
just like to act tough.

00:16:41.450 --> 00:16:44.210
We're not foolish enough
to just trust you outright.

00:16:44.500 --> 00:16:45.830
But, speaking personally,

00:16:46.420 --> 00:16:49.920
I've been to plenty of shady places,
so I know what bad dudes look like.

00:16:50.340 --> 00:16:52.880
Compared to the scum I've met,
you two are like...

00:16:52.970 --> 00:16:57.720
boys at a summer training camp
at an old school out in the boondocks.

00:16:58.140 --> 00:16:59.220
I see.

00:16:59.680 --> 00:17:01.970
Well, we have been called
"sheltered" before.

00:17:02.060 --> 00:17:03.060
Ryo.

00:17:03.140 --> 00:17:05.440
Our upbringing wasn't sheltered!

00:17:05.690 --> 00:17:07.190
It was far worse than that!

00:17:07.270 --> 00:17:08.980
Being sheltered as a kid
isn't a bad thing.

00:17:09.310 --> 00:17:10.820
You can become whatever you want.

00:17:13.240 --> 00:17:14.820
Okay, who's next?

00:17:14.900 --> 00:17:15.780
I am.

00:17:16.450 --> 00:17:20.240
My whole family made their living
by doing fortune-telling.

00:17:20.910 --> 00:17:24.500
In our palm-reading style, your left hand
tells the fate you were born with,

00:17:24.580 --> 00:17:27.540
and your right hand shows
your current fortune,

00:17:27.620 --> 00:17:28.670
so we look at both.

00:17:31.960 --> 00:17:34.050
You're quite a romantic, I see.

00:17:34.130 --> 00:17:37.430
You were a girl who lived in her own world
and dreamed many dreams.

00:17:37.800 --> 00:17:39.510
If my grandmother were here, she'd say,

00:17:39.600 --> 00:17:41.640
"You had your head in the clouds."

00:17:43.060 --> 00:17:48.100
But now your feet are on the ground
and you're trying to deal with reality.

00:17:49.150 --> 00:17:54.990
You have a strong will and your palm says
that it's finally come to the surface.

00:17:55.570 --> 00:17:56.950
Things are looking good.

00:18:01.780 --> 00:18:02.950
Wow, this is a surprise.

00:18:03.540 --> 00:18:05.950
You were very stubborn
in your younger days, yes?

00:18:06.040 --> 00:18:07.870
A bit of a spoiled brat?

00:18:08.120 --> 00:18:09.790
No way! Seriously?

00:18:11.090 --> 00:18:13.670
There were many things
that you regretted doing,

00:18:14.250 --> 00:18:15.840
then you met someone special.

00:18:15.920 --> 00:18:20.390
You opened your heart to that person
and had a pleasant time together.

00:18:20.680 --> 00:18:23.430
That experience made you who you are now.

00:18:24.180 --> 00:18:25.180
Yes.

00:18:26.520 --> 00:18:28.690
Excuse me,
do you mind if I read your palm?

00:18:29.770 --> 00:18:31.650
What can a palm actually tell you?

00:18:33.440 --> 00:18:35.610
It works best with both hands,

00:18:35.690 --> 00:18:37.900
but since you're injured,
I'll just look at your left.

00:18:38.490 --> 00:18:40.610
The left hand tells the fate
we were born with, right?

00:18:42.450 --> 00:18:43.740
What can you see?

00:18:48.620 --> 00:18:49.830
What can you see?

00:18:55.550 --> 00:18:56.420
What?

00:18:58.170 --> 00:18:59.930
Oh, it's nothing.

00:19:00.510 --> 00:19:02.470
This happens to me sometimes.

00:19:03.010 --> 00:19:06.140
I'm sorry, I can't tell anything
from just one hand after all.

00:19:06.720 --> 00:19:09.180
When your other hand is better,
please let me try again.

00:19:11.350 --> 00:19:14.190
Okay, the final performance! Go, Chimaki!

00:19:16.280 --> 00:19:19.650
This is the only talent
that I could come up with.

00:19:20.530 --> 00:19:22.280
One, two!

00:19:23.530 --> 00:19:26.950
Oh, wow. I didn't even practice for this.

00:19:27.040 --> 00:19:29.790
Dullsville! I wanted to see him fail.

00:19:29.870 --> 00:19:32.250
Hey, Natsu! You get up there and do it!

00:19:32.330 --> 00:19:33.670
What?

00:19:40.340 --> 00:19:43.930
The klutz strikes again! Hilarious!
Nice work, Natsu!

00:19:45.510 --> 00:19:46.850
Don't let him get to you.

00:19:48.470 --> 00:19:50.980
You just need decisiveness, speed,
and to pull at the right angle.

00:19:51.390 --> 00:19:53.480
Anybody can do it if they practice enough.

00:19:54.100 --> 00:19:55.610
It's nothing to feel bad about.

00:19:59.280 --> 00:20:01.200
He's just trying to act cool.

00:20:02.200 --> 00:20:05.820
The winner is Hotaru!
She gets five points.

00:20:05.950 --> 00:20:07.450
What should we do next week?

00:20:07.530 --> 00:20:08.830
How about a kanji test?

00:20:08.910 --> 00:20:10.370
Do you want to die, Arashi?

00:20:10.450 --> 00:20:13.920
Wow, Nat!
That was totally awesome just now.

00:20:14.000 --> 00:20:15.380
What brought that on?

00:20:15.460 --> 00:20:17.500
He must have fallen for you
at first sight.

00:20:17.590 --> 00:20:19.920
No, I don't think that's what it was.

00:20:20.550 --> 00:20:23.970
You never know. You should try dating him.

00:20:24.050 --> 00:20:25.090
That's crazy!

00:20:25.180 --> 00:20:28.720
Besides, I'm not interested
in dating just anybody.

00:20:32.060 --> 00:20:35.600
Well, you know, I'm not interested
in just anybody either.

00:20:36.900 --> 00:20:38.610
Oh, I'm so sorry.

00:20:39.980 --> 00:20:42.900
Though I won't deny that
I'll go for any guy who's a hunk.

00:20:43.360 --> 00:20:45.700
So, in that case, I guess
I'll set my sights on Ryo.

00:20:45.780 --> 00:20:46.820
Hey...

00:20:48.240 --> 00:20:49.790
Let's do our best, Nat!

00:20:50.580 --> 00:20:53.410
You can do it, Nat! Good night!

00:20:53.870 --> 00:20:56.210
<i>I said something
really hurtful to Matsuri.</i>

00:20:56.710 --> 00:20:58.170
<i>She might hate me now.</i>

00:20:58.590 --> 00:20:59.460
Hey.

00:21:11.600 --> 00:21:13.270
Hey! Hibari has gone missing!

00:21:13.730 --> 00:21:15.350
She left early this morning.

00:21:15.940 --> 00:21:17.730
She left? What do you mean by that?

00:21:18.060 --> 00:21:19.560
You let a child go out there alone?

00:21:19.650 --> 00:21:20.860
It's okay.

00:21:20.940 --> 00:21:22.690
Someone is with her.

00:21:23.030 --> 00:21:25.530
Her heart felt unusually at peace.

00:21:26.200 --> 00:21:27.410
Who could it be?

00:21:28.200 --> 00:21:30.620
Hibari didn't want to stay here with us.

00:21:30.700 --> 00:21:32.740
Because she hates me.

00:21:33.000 --> 00:21:34.540
Please let her do what she wants.

00:21:35.080 --> 00:21:39.580
She's a girl who is incredibly lucky
and has lots of power,

00:21:39.670 --> 00:21:41.550
but she doesn't realize it herself.

00:21:42.050 --> 00:21:43.840
That's why she's going to be just fine.

00:21:46.430 --> 00:21:47.930
You can't tap into your full potential

00:21:48.010 --> 00:21:50.010
-because you're too timid and scared.
-Is that Natsu?

00:21:50.100 --> 00:21:52.760
You're more than capable,
and we're going to show them.

00:21:52.850 --> 00:21:54.060
Right.

00:21:54.140 --> 00:21:55.930
Ango, that bastard.

00:21:56.020 --> 00:21:58.350
Looks like I'm going to have
to give him a good pounding.

00:21:59.190 --> 00:22:01.650
He'll learn to keep his hands
off our woman.

00:22:01.730 --> 00:22:02.730
Semimaru!

00:22:02.820 --> 00:22:07.240
Semimaru always treats you like dirt,
yelling at you, and beating on you.

00:22:07.320 --> 00:22:08.490
Why do you just take it?

00:22:08.910 --> 00:22:10.120
Well...

00:22:10.200 --> 00:22:12.330
That was just our comedy routine.

00:22:13.950 --> 00:22:16.120
<i>Why is he being so nice to me?</i>

00:22:16.750 --> 00:22:18.580
Hey! What are you doing over here?

00:22:18.670 --> 00:22:19.830
Practicing.

00:22:19.920 --> 00:22:21.670
Really? "Practicing," is it?

00:22:21.750 --> 00:22:22.790
Semimaru.
